repitch-kyoti rev 14 (Session 112): the PRIVATE ot_emu instrumentation behind gates 0a/0b.
Apply to a COPY of refs/octabam's tools/emu/ot_emu + vendor/{mc68k,dsp56300} in your
scratchpad -- never to the shared clone, never rebuild the shared binary or libunicorn
(memory: shared-octabam-clone-hazard). In the copy's CMakeLists.txt point OT_VENDOR at the
copied vendor dir and drop everything from "# THE GATE." down (the test targets).

  cp -R refs/octabam/tools/emu/ot_emu $S/src; cp -R refs/octabam/vendor/mc68k $S/vendor/
  rsync -a --exclude source/wxWidgets --exclude build refs/octabam/vendor/dsp56300 $S/vendor/
  (cd $S && patch -p0 < tools/repitch_ot_emu_trace.patch)   # paths below are relative to $S
  cmake -B $S/build -S $S/src && cmake --build $S/build -j8 --target ot_emu

Environment (all optional):
  RK_XWATCH=core:S:lo:hi[,...]  log every read/write of those words after arming (per PC)
  RK_XFROM=N                    arm after N host commands on the core (default 1)
  RK_XFILL=1                    fill the watched words with a canary when arming
  RK_XREPORT=FILE               the report (else stderr), written at exit
  RK_TRACE=core:pc:from:max[;...]  dump registers + RK_TRACE_MEM at each arrival at pc
  RK_TRACE_MEM=S:addr:len[,...]    what to dump;  RK_TRACE_COND=S:addr:val  only when it holds
  RK_TRACE_OUT=FILE
The vendor changes: a data-read hook in Memory::get, and DMA always copies word by word
(its memcpy fast path bypassed both hooks).
